silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_04_olog_vs_taxonomy_vs_schema_concrete_anchor_2_Taxonomy#domesticcattaxonomynode silm:hasLongDescription "The DomesticCatTaxonomyNode is the classification tree of cat species; missing verb arrows and path-equations. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Taxonomy', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
